# EXPECTATION FOR LANE RUN 23 (the re-attempt; run 22 was REFUSED at the gate) — derived and committed ALONE, BEFORE the run (D0A-R21-07).
#
# Target commit: fba091a. The instrument changes — `cp -p`, the hygiene capture, explicit
# identity counts, and the acceptance gate itself — were committed at 87d98ae, one commit
# earlier, so this prediction is about the procedure that will actually run.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHY THIS IS RUN 23 AND NOT RUN 22 AGAIN
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 22 was attempted and REFUSED by the acceptance gate; `scratch/lane-run-23/` holds its
# captured REFUSED verdict and an ATTEMPT-REFUSED record. Re-running into that directory would
# put fresh artifacts beside a retained refusal and let the verifier overwrite `acceptance.txt`
# with ACCEPTED while the refusal record still sat next to it — **a directory contradicting
# itself**, which is the same shape as the register table that survived the prose rewrite
# (D0A-R33-04/R34-04). A refused attempt is permanent record; the re-attempt gets its own number.
#
# **THE PREDICTION IS UNCHANGED AND WAS COMMITTED BEFORE RUN 22'S ATTEMPT** (75da430). No Rust
# test was added or removed since — the fixes in this range are `test-count.sh`'s set-but-empty
# refusal, the procedure's per-step env sourcing, and records. Re-measured at fba091a: unprivileged
# is still 204/26/230, so the root derivation below stands as written.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE DERIVATION
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 21 measured root 223 / 6 / 229 at d1fa4fe. ONE test identity added since, none removed
# (enumerated with `fn [a-z0-9_]+`, digits included):
#
#   every_precondition_panic_is_accompanied_by_a_side_channel_report | test_child_guard.rs | NONE
#
# Ungated — verified by grep of the 25 lines after the `fn`, and confirmed to carry `#[test]`
# rather than being a helper. It exists because the mutation campaign stopped reading the
# precondition token from output (D0A-R35-03): that is only safe while every precondition site
# reports through the side channel, so this asserts the two appear together.
#
#   EXECUTED  223 + 1 = 224
#   SKIPPED       6    =   6      (nothing added or removed is gated)
#   reported  229 + 1 = 230       (agrees with the measured unprivileged 204/26/230)
#
# Cross-check: unprivileged went 203/26/229 -> 204/26/230, i.e. +1 executed and +0 skipped —
# the same partition of the same test. Any other root figure falsifies one of these two
# statements, and the mismatch is the result.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE VERIFIER'S VERDICT *IS* THE RUN'S ACCEPTANCE — it is not a check on the run
# =========================================================================================
#
# `scripts/lane-accept.py scratch/lane-run-23` runs LAST and decides whether this run may be
# cited as merge acceptance. **If it refuses, the run is not accepted regardless of what the
# counts say.** A green 224/6/230 with a REFUSED verdict is an unaccepted run, and recording it
# any other way would recreate the exact defect the tool exists to close — a required check
# whose failure changes nothing (`DEFECT_CLASSES` 54).
#
# It executes nothing. The procedure still runs by hand, unchanged. The verifier reads only what
# the steps retained.
#
# **This is its first real use.** It has been run against lane run 21, which it REFUSED for two
# genuine gaps (no hygiene capture; identities written without counts). Both are fixed in the
# procedure for this run, so run 23 is the first that can be ACCEPTED rather than refused — run 22 never
# reached the count at all.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHAT A REFUSAL WOULD MEAN AT EACH CHECK — three different findings, one of them surprising
# =========================================================================================
#
# 1. **MISSING artifact** (hygiene.txt, a hash file, the status file, the transcript, the
#    identity lists, the control observation). Means a retention step did not run, or ran and
#    wrote nowhere. **A finding about the PROCEDURE or about my handover of it** — which is
#    where three of class 54's four instances came from. Not surprising; expected to be the
#    most likely refusal on a first use.
#
# 2. **FAILING artifact** (a nonzero producer exit, hashes that differ across the forced
#    rebuild, mismatched helper digests, a PAM mismatch, a stale session, a non-zero identity
#    difference, free space short). Means **a real condition the lane is supposed to catch**,
#    and the verifier is doing exactly what it was built for. A failing hash pair in particular
#    would mean the executables were STALE and the run measured code that is not this tree's —
#    that is a finding about the RUN, and the counts from it would be void.
#
# 3. **MISORDERED artifacts** — specifically `hashes-after` newer than `root-run.log`, i.e.
#    **freshness proven AFTER the run rather than before it.** This is the one that would be
#    SURPRISING, and it is the one no count or content check can see: the artifacts would all be
#    present and all internally valid, and the run would still prove nothing about the binaries
#    it executed. It is "closed-after is not run" one level up. If this fires, suspect the
#    retention step before the run — `cp` without `-p` produces exactly this signature, and
#    that is how the verifier justified itself on its first execution, refusing artifacts
#    written minutes earlier.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE LIMIT, STATED BEFORE THE RUN SO A GREEN CANNOT IMPLY MORE THAN IT COVERS
# =========================================================================================
#
# **The verifier cannot bind these artifacts to a commit.** Nothing in `scratch/lane-run-22/`
# says which tree produced it. An ACCEPTED verdict establishes that every required step ran, in
# the right order, and passed — it does NOT establish that they ran against the tree being
# merged. The run record carries the SHA and a reader must still check it. This is stated in the
# tool's own docstring and repeated here because a verdict that reads as "the run is good"
# invites exactly the over-read this arc keeps producing.
#
# Two further limits carried forward: Part B's control has produced only `Reached`, and
# `Topology`/`Scan`/`Unresolved` have never been produced at root; and **reaping is still
# never independently observed** — the only reaping evidence is the daemon's own exit status.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=224
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=6
EXPECTED_REPORTED=230
